# RC-001 — Reveal & Reading Experience

North star: **"I've finished something meaningful."**

## Before changing select → reveal → reading ask

- Does this feel like one continuous ritual, not three screens?
- Does the reveal pause naturally without feeling slow or game-like?
- Does reading hierarchy guide the eye (identity → core → depth → reflection → close)?
- Are long texts readable without condense truncation?
- Does performance stay smooth (ambient isolated from content rebuilds)?

If any answer is no — revise.

## Canonical doc

`docs/RC-001.md`

## Out of scope

Home redesign · navigation changes · new features

## Success

Ceremonial reveal, clear reading hierarchy, peaceful close — one experience.
